# B08: Storage Engine Quota Guard & Read/Write Audit Decorator (`StorageDecorator`)

This module implements a storage decorator (`TrackedStorage`) with capacity quota enforcement (`quota_bytes`) and read/write audit telemetry counters.
Its `invariant` guarantees that `used_bytes` never exceeds `quota_bytes`, and `ensures` verifies exact updates to audit counters and used capacity after each read or write operation.

```jenny
module storage_decorator

pub enum StorageError {
    QuotaExceeded,
    InvalidPayloadSize,
    InvalidQuota,
}

pub struct TrackedStorage {
    pub quota_bytes: usize,
    pub used_bytes: usize = 0,
    pub read_ops: usize = 0,
    pub write_ops: usize = 0,

    invariant {
        self.quota_bytes > 0
        self.used_bytes <= self.quota_bytes
    }
}

impl TrackedStorage {
    pub fn new(quota_bytes: usize) -> TrackedStorage ! StorageError
        requires quota_bytes > 0 else StorageError.InvalidQuota
        ensures result.used_bytes == 0
        ensures result.write_ops == 0

    pub fn write_block(mut self, payload_bytes: usize) -> usize ! StorageError
        requires payload_bytes > 0 else StorageError.InvalidPayloadSize
        requires self.used_bytes + payload_bytes <= self.quota_bytes else StorageError.QuotaExceeded
        ensures self.write_ops == old(self.write_ops) + 1
        ensures self.used_bytes == old(self.used_bytes) + payload_bytes

    pub fn read_block(mut self) -> usize
        ensures self.read_ops == old(self.read_ops) + 1
        ensures result == self.used_bytes
}

@example("EX-B08-01: storage quota tracking and telemetry counters") {
    var store = TrackedStorage.new(1024)!
    val u1 = store.write_block(256)!
    assert(u1 == 256)
    assert(store.write_ops == 1)

    val u2 = store.write_block(512)!
    assert(u2 == 768)
    assert(store.write_ops == 2)

    val r1 = store.read_block()
    assert(r1 == 768)
    assert(store.read_ops == 1)
}

@example("EX-B08-02: reject quota overflow and empty writes") {
    var store = TrackedStorage.new(500)!
    store.write_block(400)!

    val over_err = store.write_block(200)
    assert(over_err is StorageError.QuotaExceeded)
    assert(store.used_bytes == 400)

    val zero_err = store.write_block(0)
    assert(zero_err is StorageError.InvalidPayloadSize)
}
```
